<LICENCE_NOT_CHOSEN>

This project has not chosen a licence yet, and CI is red until it does.

That is deliberate. An unlicensed public repository grants no rights at all --
more restrictive than almost anyone intends -- and choosing is the one decision
a bootstrap script cannot make for you. Replace this entire file with the full
text of your chosen licence.

Common choices:

  MIT           Shortest permissive licence in common use. Use, modify and
                redistribute, including commercially, provided the notice is
                kept. No patent grant.

  Apache-2.0    Permissive, plus an explicit patent grant and a NOTICE
                mechanism, and requires stating changes. Preferred where
                patents or corporate consumers matter.

  GPL-3.0       Copyleft: derivative works must also be GPL-3.0. Choose it to
                require that downstream stays open.

  Proprietary   All rights reserved. Say so explicitly rather than leaving the
                repository unlicensed, so the intent is stated rather than
                inferred.

Ticket D5 explains this; https://choosealicense.com/ compares them properly.
